@startuml
title Proposed story: save a student's career goal
skinparam shadowing false
actor Student
boundary "Career goal interface\n(proposed backend-connected UI)" as UI
control "Career goal service\n(proposed)" as Service
participant "Prisma Client\n(data access)" as ORM
database "SQLite\n(proposed persistence)" as DB

note over UI,DB
  Proposed flow, not implemented: today's UI uses localStorage.
  A future backend must establish the student's identity and authorize
  access before writing; authentication is not yet designed.
end note

Student -> UI: Select or clear roadmap / employer
UI -> Service: Save both selections for current student\n(nullable roadmapId and employerProfileId)
activate Service
Service -> Service: Authorize student; validate supported IDs\nand allow either selection to be empty
alt Invalid selection or unauthorized request
  Service --> UI: Report validation / authorization error
  UI --> Student: Show error; do not report a saved goal
else Valid selection
  Service -> ORM: Upsert StudentCareerGoal by unique studentId\n(create or update both selection IDs)
  activate ORM
  ORM -> DB: Write goal (FK and unique constraints)
  activate DB
  alt Write succeeds
    DB --> ORM: Stored goal
    ORM --> Service: Stored goal
    Service --> UI: Return saved selections
    UI --> Student: Display saved career goal
  else Write fails
    DB --> ORM: Constraint or database error
    ORM --> Service: Error
    Service --> UI: Report save failure
    UI --> Student: Show save failure
  end
  deactivate DB
  deactivate ORM
end
deactivate Service
@enduml
